// wdoc section: Styling (classes + themes).

// Preview-only class used in the "Authoring" live example below. Declared at
// the top level so it applies site-wide; hyphenated names must be quoted.
class "sty-accent" {
  color = "#bf616a"
  bold  = true
  dark  { color = "#88c0d0" }
  light { color = "#5e81ac" }
}

page wdoc_styling { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Styling"

  p "Two layers control how a site looks: `class` blocks style individual elements, and a site `theme` sets the palette every built-in element draws from. Classes always win over theme defaults via the cascade, so you theme broadly and override locally."

  h2 "Classes"

  p "A `class <name> { … }` block declares a CSS class. Apply it by listing the name in any block's `class` field (or a span's). Fields cover text, box, and SVG paint properties; per-mode overrides go in `dark { }` / `light { }` sub-blocks."

  h3 "Authoring"

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
class accent {
  color = "var(--wdoc-accent)"
  bold  = true
  dark  { color = "#88c0d0" }
  light { color = "#5e81ac" }
}

// Use the class on a span:
text {
  span "highlighted segment" { class = ["accent"] }
}
WCL
  }

  p "Live — the `sty-accent` class declared at the top of this page, applied to a span (and following the light/dark mode):"

  diagram { width = 460  height = 90
    card { x = 16.0  y = 12.0  width = 428.0  height = 66.0
      text {
        span "Plain text, then a "
        span "highlighted segment" { class = ["sty-accent"] }
        span " styled by a class."
      }
    }
  }

  h3 "Field groups"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Group" | "Fields" |
      | "Text"  | "`color`, `background`, `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `font_size`, `font_family`, `text_align`, `text_transform`, `letter_spacing`, `line_height`" |
      | "Box"   | "`padding`, `margin`, `border`" |
      | "SVG"   | "`fill`, `stroke`, `stroke_width`, `stroke_linejoin`, `stroke_linecap`, `opacity`" |
      | "Callout" | "`accent` — sets a callout's accent colour (heading, border, icon) when the class is on a `callout`" |
      | "Modes" | "`dark { … }`, `light { … }` for prefers-color-scheme overrides" |
  }

  h3 "Hyphenated names"

  p "Class names that contain hyphens (or any non-identifier character) must be quoted: `class \"wdoc-series-1\" { fill = \"#88c0d0\" }`. This is how you override built-in classes like the chart palette or callout styles."

  callout "Site scope" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "Set sites = [:foo] on a class to scope it to one site in a multi-site document. Omit the field and the class applies everywhere."
  }

  h2 "Themes"

  p "A theme is a complete colour palette plus the rules that map it onto every built-in element — page background, links, headings, code, charts, callouts, tables, inline emphasis. Selecting a theme in one line recolours the whole site."

  h3 "Selecting a built-in theme"

  p "Set `theme = :<name>` on a `site` — a symbol naming a `theme` block. Seven built-in palettes ship, each with co-ordinated dark and light variants. `theme_toggle = true` adds a light/dark toggle button to the chrome."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
site mysite {
  default_template = :book
  theme            = :tokyonight
  accent           = :cyan
  theme_toggle     = true
}
WCL
  }

  h3 "Built-in themes"

  table {
    rows:
      | "Theme"        | "Notes" |
      | "`nord`"       | "Cool blue-grey, the default" |
      | "`gruvbox`"    | "Warm retro" |
      | "`solarized`"  | "Classic Solarized" |
      | "`catppuccin`" | "Soft pastel" |
      | "`tokyonight`" | "Vivid night palette" |
      | "`kanagawa`"   | "Muted with hints of indigo" |
      | "`everforest`" | "Green forest tones" |
  }

  h3 "Accent colour"

  p "Independently of the theme, `accent = :cyan` (or `:red`/`:orange`/`:yellow`/`:green`/`:blue`/`:purple`/`:pink`) picks the hue used for links and current-chapter highlights. Default is `:blue`."

  h3 "Custom themes"

  p "A theme is just a `theme` block holding a `dark` and a `light` `palette` sub-block; select it with `theme = :name`. Each palette sets any of the 18 colour roles (documented in `lib/theme.wcl`); omitted roles fall back through the cascade."

  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
theme sunset {
  palette dark {
    bg = "#1a1a2e"  fg = "#e0e0e0"
    blue = "#5e81ac"  green = "#a3be8c"
    // … any of the 18 roles
  }
  palette light {
    bg = "#fdf6e3"  fg = "#073642"
  }
}

site mysite { theme = :sunset  accent = :blue }
WCL
  }
}
